 that he's just another freelance writer now?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bear in mind that Onyx Path only has five full-time employees: Rich Thomas, Lisa Thomas, Mike Chaney, Rose Bailey, and Matt McElroy. All of the rest of us -- from social media to editing to artists to indexers to writers to developers -- are &quot;just&quot; freelancers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T06:50:19-08:00","id":1060851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1060634#post1060634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's working on horror games of his own that look quite exciting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You couldn't throw out some more specifics there? (I mean that as a request, not snark).<br /> <br /> Sad to see Dave Hill go from OPP though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T08:07:49-08:00","id":1060880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1060851#post1060851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You couldn't throw out some more specifics there? (I mean that as a request, not snark).<br /> <br /> Sad to see Dave Hill go from OPP though.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's been posting excerpts and tidbits on his personal FB page, and he just started a page for the game series, which is called <i>More Than Night. </i>Mena wrote a short story that he posted this morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T11:01:03-08:00","id":1060940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1060880#post1060880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's been posting excerpts and tidbits on his personal FB page, and he just started a page for the game series, which is called <i>More Than Night. </i>Mena wrote a short story that he posted this morning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks v much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:35:00-07:00","id":1077132,"title":"","content":"I'm even more excited to see where Changeling 2E goes now that Rose is the developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:36:38-07:00","id":1077133,"title":"","content":"Changeling 2e isn't going to be the game I was looking forward to any more, given how much of David's work has apparently been cut out. Pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:58:09-07:00","id":1077147,"title":"","content":"I'm just looking forwards to how Changeling 2e goes; while I am excited for what the previous previews showed me, I'm also keeping an open mind for how the game will end up. It's like playing the Beta of a videogame; you may like what's in there, and sad when it's changed, but overall there will be more stuff in the full game than the Beta and that's something to love too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:37:00-07:00","id":1077232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077147#post1077147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just looking forwards to how Changeling 2e goes; while I am excited for what the previous previews showed me, I'm also keeping an open mind for how the game will end up. It's like playing the Beta of a videogame; you may like what's in there, and sad when it's changed, but overall there will be more stuff in the full game than the Beta and that's something to love too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except we had 90% of game (and there was already 100% of the game that David sent to onyx path), betas are normally iterative design but this is &quot;let's scrap the major foundations of this already complete game&quot;. <br /> <br /> Also videogame betas normally don't change tone between updates unless the previous tone wasn't intentional... And David's tone was definitely completely intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:41:46-07:00","id":1077234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077133#post1077133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling 2e isn't going to be the game I was looking forward to any more, given how much of David's work has apparently been cut out. Pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe wait until you see the finished version before you decide it's not going to be for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:48:25-07:00","id":1077238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077234#post1077234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe wait until you see the finished version before you decide it's not going to be for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... Not how purchasing things works.<br /> If you're not interested in a product why would you buy it to see if it can convince you to be interested rather than spending that money on things you are interested in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:55:49-07:00","id":1077241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077238#post1077238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's... Not how purchasing things works.<br /> If you're not interested in a product why would you buy it to see if it can convince you to be interested rather than spending that money on things you are interested in?</div> </div> </div> </div>I take a punt on books all the time. It's a good way of exposing yourself to new writers and ideas.<br /> <br /> It seems to me to be a little bit of a knee-jerk reaction to say &quot;this author's not on this collaborative piece anymore, so I'm out,&quot; or words to that effect. Still, it's a buyer's market.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:01:53-07:00","id":1077247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077241#post1077241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take a punt on books all the time. It's a good way of exposing yourself to new writers and ideas.<br /> <br /> It seems to me to be a little bit of a knee-jerk reaction to say &quot;this author's not on this collaborative piece anymore, so I'm out,&quot; or words to that effect. Still, it's a buyer's market.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a bit different to just &quot;this author's not on this collaborative piece anymore\u201d, as the author in question was the line developer and that his removal has lead to many changes which can easily not be to someone's taste if they preferred the old tone/aesthetic.<br /> <br /> I myself am being cautious about the new version and am unsure on whether to purchase it yet since David's philosophy on beauty from darkness and mental health are identical to my own. I might still purchase it, but I'll be waiting to see how much of the games philosophy has changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-12-2017, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:04:32-07:00","id":1077249,"title":"","content":"To be clear, if we'd received a finished manuscript for the CtL2 core, we'd likely have gone to press with it. As is, we're finishing the writing and development process. There's both all-new content and elements from earlier drafts.<br /> <br /> And, of course, like any CofD book, once it's all out, go ahead and use whatever sources work for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:07:38-07:00","id":1077253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077241#post1077241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take a punt on books all the time. It's a good way of exposing yourself to new writers and ideas.<br /> <br /> It seems to me to be a little bit of a knee-jerk reaction to say &amp;quot;this author's not on this collaborative piece anymore, so I'm out,&amp;quot; or words to that effect. Still, it's a buyer's market.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't exactly a fair comparison to what Lex is saying. We've seen 80% of a project and gotten hyped for it over more than a year. Now we've heard the guy who developed that project is no longer involved in it. And the new developers are previewing content that goes over the same material we've already seen, and it's completely different. This isn't &quot;this writer is no longer on this collaborative piece any more&quot; this is &quot;the product is completely changing and I am not liking what I've seen of this new product as much as I like the previous one I was being shown, so I'm not going to buy it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:15:41-07:00","id":1077260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077253#post1077253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't exactly a fair comparison to what Lex is saying. We've seen 80% of a project and gotten hyped for it over more than a year. Now we've heard the guy who developed that project is no longer involved in it. And the new developers are previewing content that goes over the same material we've already seen, and it's completely different. This isn't &quot;this writer is no longer on this collaborative piece any more&quot; this is &quot;the product is completely changing and I am not liking what I've seen of this new product as much as I like the previous one I was being shown, so I'm not going to buy it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Well fair enough. If Lex doesn't like the previews, she may not like the finished product. Time will tell!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:16:27-07:00","id":1077261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077249#post1077249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, if we'd received a finished manuscript for the CtL2 core, we'd likely have gone to press with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... Maybe I'm misunderstanding what you mean by a finished manuscript, but I thought you did? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/985239-very-minor-but-also-major-update#post985239\">According to David</a>, he sent all of his stuff in for approval in October. Those drafts are also still out there, in case the email got misplaced or something. I know there's a thread where all the drafted content David had previewed is compiled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:21:39-07:00","id":1077269,"title":"","content":"I'll grant that it was quite a bit of content but that stuff is hardly a manuscript let alone a polished manuscript ready to go to print.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, there was new content previewed somewhere? Can someone add the link in this thread. I've obviously missed a few developments while prepping to defend my dissertation proposal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:23:04-07:00","id":1077270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077269#post1077269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll grant that it was quite a bit of content but that stuff is hardly a manuscript let alone a polished manuscript ready to go to print.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, there was new content previewed somewhere? Can someone add the link in this thread. I've obviously missed a few developments while prepping to defend my dissertation proposal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's on theonyxpath.com under the Changeling: The Lost tag. A bunch of development blog posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:24:55-07:00","id":1077271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077253#post1077253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't exactly a fair comparison to what Lex is saying. We've seen 80% of a project and gotten hyped for it over more than a year. Now we've heard the guy who developed that project is no longer involved in it. And the new developers are previewing content that goes over the same material we've already seen, and it's completely different. This isn't &quot;this writer is no longer on this collaborative piece any more&quot; this is &quot;the product is completely changing and I am not liking what I've seen of this new product as much as I like the previous one I was being shown, so I'm not going to buy it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair we live in a world with people who have not just balked at less than 20% of a game, but gone on to devote significant portions of their lives to ensuring that no one uses any part of a game because they didn't like a paragraph. As great as open development is, the finished product is what's ultimately going to matter. Though as Rose points out, the open development work is still there and can be used, and likely fit into Changeling without too much change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:28:03-07:00","id":1077275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077269#post1077269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll grant that it was quite a bit of content but that stuff is hardly a manuscript let alone a polished manuscript ready to go to print.</div> </div> </div> </div>The playtest previews? No, that was far from a manuscript. I don't imagine that was what David was talking about when he said he had sent the compiled drafts in for approval though. What that says to me was that all of the writing for the book was done and in to OP to be rubberstamped and pushed on to art direction, so it seems a little strange to me to now here they would have gone forward with his version if it had been finished. Pretty sure it was finished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:28:18-07:00","id":1077276,"title":"","content":"...this is going to turn into the Beast KS draft vs Finalized Draft debacle, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Goody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:30:34-07:00","id":1077279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077276#post1077276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...this is going to turn into the Beast KS draft vs Finalized Draft debacle, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably less so, since people aren't effectively 'pre-ordering' the game or supporting it with backer money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:32:03-07:00","id":1077280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077271#post1077271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair we live in a world with people who have not just balked at less than 20% of a game, but gone on to devote significant portions of their lives to ensuring that no one uses any part of a game because they didn't like a paragraph. As great as open development is, the finished product is what's ultimately going to matter. Though as Rose points out, the open development work is still there and can be used, and likely fit into Changeling without too much change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no doubt. I'm just saying, I can't really blame Lex for not being onboard with the new direction. I myself am withholding judgment until I've seen more of the new game, but I still don't think it's fair to accuse Lex of deciding not to buy Lost simply because a writer on the project is no longer involved. This is a more significant change than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:35:12-07:00","id":1077281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077269#post1077269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll grant that it was quite a bit of content but that stuff is hardly a manuscript let alone a polished manuscript ready to go to print.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there's a large functional difference between what was previewed and the finished manuscript needed for the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:38:47-07:00","id":1077288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077280#post1077280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, no doubt. I'm just saying, I can't really blame Lex for not being onboard with the new direction. I myself am withholding judgment until I've seen more of the new game, but I still don't think it's fair to accuse Lex of deciding not to buy Lost simply because a writer on the project is no longer involved. This is a more significant change than that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It absolutely is. And like Rose says, what was turned in was not a finished manuscript.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:48:27-07:00","id":1077296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077288#post1077288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It absolutely is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It absolutely is a bigger change, or if absolutely is fair to accuse Lex of making her decision not to buy the game based solely on a writer no longer being involved in the project? Cause I can't agree if it's the latter. That would be fair if, say, Sean had pulled out and the Paris section was no longer going to be in the book. But David was not just a writer on the project, he was the developer, and we have seen from the previews of the latest drafts that there are some significant changes being made. If she doesn't like what she's seeing in the new drafts, that's a factor beyond David's lack of involvement going into her decision. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077288#post1077288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And like Rose says, what was turned in was not a finished manuscript.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I don't know the details of what goes on behind the scenes, just seemed odd to me since it sounded like the writing for his version had been completed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:54:07-07:00","id":1077301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077296#post1077296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It absolutely is a bigger change, or if absolutely is fair to accuse Lex of making her decision not to buy the game based solely on a writer no longer being involved in the project? Cause I can't agree if it's the latter. <br /> <br /> Fair enough. I don't know the details of what goes on behind the scenes, just seemed odd to me since it sounded like the writing for his version had been completed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The former. <br /> <br /> Look, would it be helpful to people if I did a blog post and did a &quot;how the sausage is made&quot; on how a book goes from inception to publication? 'Cause there are a lot of little details and twists/turns that y'all don't know about (because why would you?) and they're important, but without context they'll sound...kind of thin.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:00:31-07:00","id":1077307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077301#post1077301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, would it be helpful to people if I did a blog post and did a &quot;how the sausage is made&quot; on how a book goes from inception to publication? 'Cause there are a lot of little details and twists/turns that y'all don't know about (because why would you?) and they're important, but without context they'll sound...kind of thin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one would find that very interesting, independent of any drama here in the Lost forums! It's always fascinating to get the behind the scenes look.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:03:51-07:00","id":1077310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077301#post1077301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The former.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, cool. Guess I needn't have made a pre-emptive counter-argument against the latter. sorry!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077301#post1077301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, would it be helpful to people if I did a blog post and did a &quot;how the sausage is made&quot; on how a book goes from inception to publication? 'Cause there are a lot of little details and twists/turns that y'all don't know about (because why would you?) and they're important, but without context they'll sound...kind of thin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sure wouldn't say no to seeing such a thing. That said, I expect those of us who are worried about the new direction won't be settled by anything save a run-down of what we can expect <i>won't</i> be changing significantly. We've been told a few times that some stuff is staying the same, but all that is getting previewed is stuff that's been completely re-written, and that's scary for those of us who fell in love with David's drafts. I would be a lot less worried if I knew whether or not Clarity is being completely wre-written, for example, or whether Kiths will still work the same way. Even if the answer is that my favorite parts are changing, at least I can mentally prepare myself for that instead of just sitting here wondering what thing that I loved from David's drafts will get axed next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-12-2017, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:05:23-07:00","id":1077311,"title":"","content":"Oh, and in case it needed saying: if you don't like the material, I certainly don't think you're obligated to buy it. Part of the point of showing things in advance is to help people make informed purchasing decisions. And building on that, one of the core ideas of the CofD is that you should be able to imagine and play the game in the ways you choose. I put my heart and soul into these worlds, but no one needs to take a loyalty pledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:15:04-07:00","id":1077318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077310#post1077310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, cool. Guess I needn't have made a pre-emptive counter-argument against the latter. sorry!<br /> <br /> <br /> I sure wouldn't say no to seeing such a thing. That said, I expect those of us who are worried about the new direction won't be settled by anything save a run-down of what we can expect <i>won't</i> be changing significantly. We've been told a few times that some stuff is staying the same, but all that is getting previewed is stuff that's been completely re-written, and that's scary for those of us who fell in love with David's drafts. I would be a lot less worried if I knew whether or not Clarity is being completely wre-written, for example, or whether Kiths will still work the same way. Even if the answer is that my favorite parts are changing, at least I can mentally prepare myself for that instead of just sitting here wondering what thing that I loved from David's drafts will get axed next.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this. Uncertainty is the biggest issue right now. Knowing what was changing and what isn't, even tentatively, would help a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:47:20-07:00","id":1077394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077310#post1077310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sure wouldn't say no to seeing such a thing. That said, I expect those of us who are worried about the new direction won't be settled by anything save a run-down of what we can expect <i>won't</i> be changing significantly. We've been told a few times that some stuff is staying the same, but all that is getting previewed is stuff that's been completely re-written, and that's scary for those of us who fell in love with David's drafts. I would be a lot less worried if I knew whether or not Clarity is being completely wre-written, for example, or whether Kiths will still work the same way. Even if the answer is that my favorite parts are changing, at least I can mentally prepare myself for that instead of just sitting here wondering what thing that I loved from David's drafts will get axed next.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is why I stopped doing open dev on material that I don't own start to finish.<br /> <br /> Here's a harsh truth: David doesn't own the IP any more than I own <b>Promethean</b> or <b>Beast</b>. He signed a contract that said &quot;work for hire,&quot; and that means OPP is where the buck stops, not him. That means that, yes, while he can post on the blog and say &quot;here's what I'm planning,&quot; it's not real until it goes to press. If Onyx Path changes something, <i>especially</i> so late in the game, there's a reason for it, and it's not something as petty or personal as &quot;yeah, fuck that guy.&quot;<br /> <br /> (See also: <b>Beast</b> getting a revision very late in the game. It needed it.)*<br /> <br /> Anyway, to your general question, Rose and Meghan are the devs, and so they're going to be the ones to tell you what's changed and how.<br /> <br /> *I want to clarify this: <b>Beast</b> needed the revision. My vision for the game didn't come through the way I wanted it to (there are reasons for that, but buy me a drink at GenCon and ask me), OPP saw that, I agreed, we went back into development. It was not by any means a decision I disagreed with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","user":"blackhatmatt","date":". 04-12-2017, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:59:04-07:00","id":1077401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077394#post1077394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, this is why I stopped doing open dev on material that I don't own start to finish. <br /> <br /> Here's a harsh truth: David doesn't own the IP any more than I own <b>Promethean</b> or <b>Beast</b>. He signed a contract that said &amp;quot;work for hire,&amp;quot; and that means OPP is where the buck stops, not him. That means that, yes, while he can post on the blog and say &amp;quot;here's what I'm planning,&amp;quot; it's not real until it goes to press. If Onyx Path changes something, <i>especially</i> so late in the game, there's a reason for it, and it's not something as petty or personal as &amp;quot;yeah, fuck that guy.&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> (See also: <b>Beast</b> getting a revision very late in the game. It needed it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sure. To be clear, I get there are reasons for the change of hands, and while I'm not thrilled with the whole situation, I'm not like &quot;fuck Onyx Path&quot;, nor do I assume they're like &quot;fuck David Hill&quot;. I'm disappointed that the game I was super stoked for is changing, but I'll get over it. And it's not like those drafts David worked on are going anywhere, if I want to run that game I can. I'm just saying as one of the fans who is sad to see the game changing so much, knowing what not to hope won't change would help me feel more secure. And I think it would help us avoid this situation where the fandom has a collective freakout every time there's a new development blog. I know Onyx Path doesn't owe us that, but I still want to express that I think it would be a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077394#post1077394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, to your general question, Rose and Meghan are the devs, and so they're going to be the ones to tell you what's changed and how.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. I hope they decide to let us know. If not, we'll deal, but I'mma be pretty anxious until I have a better idea what's changing and what isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:59:50-07:00","id":1077402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077301#post1077301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The former. <br /> <br /> Look, would it be helpful to people if I did a blog post and did a &amp;quot;how the sausage is made&amp;quot; on how a book goes from inception to publication? 'Cause there are a lot of little details and twists/turns that y'all don't know about (because why would you?) and they're important, but without context they'll sound...kind of thin.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly yes, because I think a lot us are confused by what's going on, and many of us really liked the vision David Hill and his team were presenting and so are worried that their favourite parts are now gone. <br /> <br /> In addition a basic explanation of where Changeling is now would be good because many of us are confused and worried. <br /> <br /> Are Seemings still about achieving personal agency and kiths about your durance for example? Do we still have around a hundred kiths or we're many of them cut? <br /> <br /> Honestly just a basic outline of what's still in from David Hill's version and what's changed or completely new would go along ways to resolving people's concerns. Just a basic idea, not massively detailed even. <br /> <br /> Like is his dreamwalking system in, or has it been changed, do we have the courts for Toronto, Honshu, Miami, and Paris are still, is Embracing the Wyrd still a thing, and so on. You don't have to even get highly detailed. <br /> <br /> It's just that David Hill's approach to Changeling has it's fans so I think this could pacify people. This whole thing has been shocking, especially where it happened in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:00:22-07:00","id":1077403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077401#post1077401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, sure. To be clear, I get there are reasons for the change of hands, and while I'm not thrilled with the whole situation, I'm not like &quot;fuck Onyx Path&quot;, nor do I assume they're like &quot;fuck David Hill&quot;. I'm disappointed that the game I was super stoked for is changing, but I'll get over it. And it's not like those drafts David worked on are going anywhere, if I want to run that game I can. I'm just saying as one of the fans who is sad to see the game changing so much, knowing what not to hope won't change would help me feel more secure. And I think it would help us avoid this situation where the fandom has a collective freakout every time there's a new development blog. I know Onyx Path doesn't owe us that, but I still want to express that I think it would be a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell you one thing I've learned after doing this for 20 years: Getting the collective fandom to freak out is about as difficult a task as putting on a hat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:01:33-07:00","id":1077404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077311#post1077311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and in case it needed saying: if you don't like the material, I certainly don't think you're obligated to buy it. Part of the point of showing things in advance is to help people make informed purchasing decisions. And building on that, one of the core ideas of the CofD is that you should be able to imagine and play the game in the ways you choose. I put my heart and soul into these worlds, but no one needs to take a loyalty pledge.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for that, it's a fair way to do business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-12-2017, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:04:56-07:00","id":1077409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077301#post1077301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The former.<br /> <br /> Look, would it be helpful to people if I did a blog post and did a &quot;how the sausage is made&quot; on how a book goes from inception to publication? 'Cause there are a lot of little details and twists/turns that y'all don't know about (because why would you?) and they're important, but without context they'll sound...kind of thin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like a potentially interesting read, but I doubt it would help. The reasonable response to the situation is confusion. There was a bit of miscommunication. I think 80% finished was the given figure before the team change and when David Hill said he was finished there was no indication at the time that did not mean the book was finished as it usually would be. The announcement came later. I think the book moving around on the blurbs or whatever RichT calls it didn't help clarify anything. I really don't think everyone has fully processed the situation. A significant portion of the book is core rules so was finished before there was a first team. The unfinished part is all new or revised so it is unrealistic to expect a new team to come in and continue with the old vision which wasn't even crystallized yet. Your idea isn't bad. I just don't believe the people that it could help the most would be receptive.<br /> <br /> It's an awkward situation. The team should keep pushing through and putting forth their best effort as they have. Hopefully, it will work out. Only time will help, along with quality work. Plenty of books are in the pipe so Changeling doesn't need to be rushed out. Feelings might change after the anthology comes out. We shall see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:06:23-07:00","id":1077411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077403#post1077403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tell you one thing I've learned after doing this for 20 years: Getting the collective fandom to freak out is about as difficult a task as putting on a hat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, true that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:10:56-07:00","id":1077416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077318#post1077318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So much this. Uncertainty is the biggest issue right now. Knowing what was changing and what isn't, even tentatively, would help a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div> Exactly I think people could far more easily make their peace with the changes if they had a better idea of what changed and didn't change, it's the not knowing that causing people aniexity and worry. <br /> <br /> Like I can make peace with the Seasonal Courts getting more attention in Chapter 1 and Bulwarks and Approaches being gone, but it's not knowing what else is gone, changed, or new in broad strokes that has me concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:12:16-07:00","id":1077417,"title":"","content":"Irony, I actually had Sausage for dinner tonight before reading that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:16:47-07:00","id":1077421,"title":"","content":"<i>Changeling</i> is currently at the end of second drafts for the new stuff. Meghan and I will be sharing more material as we finish our development passes on it, and as needs like spot playtesting or reconciling different chapters are addressed. I'm trying to make sure that anything I say about the game is something I can back up with a piece of the book that's already solidly in place. There's room to change and tweak -- for example, there was some good discussion on RPGnet about Court recruitment that Ethan's going to follow up on, and I'm looking at what we can add for custom Court powers beyond the Mantle mechanics we've been using from earlier drafts. But, globally speaking, I want to present things that are near-finished and that embody the game we'll be delivering to you.<br /> <br /> Please be patient as we get things squared away -- forum discussions can evolve much more quickly than I can produce a finished book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:35:24-07:00","id":1077436,"title":"","content":"Since it was brought up, it hasn't gone unnoticed that some (multiple) developers don't like open development for reasons (I will leave that to them and keep my speculation to myself). My advice is not to do what you don't want to do. It seldom comes out as well as it should. Actually, it might even be best to just call it a development blog and indicate a specific offering as open when that is desired. The only guaranteed response to open development is the same as a finished and not quite proofed book, criticism. Obviously, that isn't going to be desirable to everyone. Nobody should be putting up with shit. Life is too short. Some developers only want to use blogs to promote a book and that is fine, as long as the intent is clearly just to draw people in. Developers and writers are only obligated to put out product and that is solely because that is what they are paid to do. The rest is gravy. If someone can't understand volunteer work is not obligatory, fuck that. All developers and writers should enjoy their work so everybody wins. Happy team, better product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:48:47-07:00","id":1077447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077421#post1077421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Changeling</i> is currently at the end of second drafts for the new stuff. Meghan and I will be sharing more material as we finish our development passes on it, and as needs like spot playtesting or reconciling different chapters are addressed. I'm trying to make sure that anything I say about the game is something I can back up with a piece of the book that's already solidly in place. There's room to change and tweak -- for example, there was some good discussion on RPGnet about Court recruitment that Ethan's going to follow up on, and I'm looking at what we can add for custom Court powers beyond the Mantle mechanics we've been using from earlier drafts. But, globally speaking, I want to present things that are near-finished and that embody the game we'll be delivering to you.<br /> <br /> Please be patient as we get things squared away -- forum discussions can evolve much more quickly than I can produce a finished book.</div> </div> </div> </div> That sounds reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:58:19-07:00","id":1077452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077421#post1077421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm looking at what we can add for custom Court powers beyond the Mantle mechanics we've been using from earlier drafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing that without getting a situation like vampire's Covenants where you have to make tonnes of content if your want to use a faction system other then the default sounds difficult. Will be interesting to see what the result is in the end.<br /> <br /> Though I'm surprised that mantle's, approaches, and court contracts weren't considered enough to have each court feel like it had its own powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T21:49:48-07:00","id":1077515,"title":"","content":"I like open development, and this company can be great about it. I was there when Mummy was being talked about, and the end product represented what the developers and fans talked about. Some developers are more interactive than others, but so far, open development has always been fun, and always gets me excited for a product.<br /> <br /> While I was nervous about Bulwark being axed as a mechanic (if it has. I have a feeling its in the air, and its a tough decision and part of the open development process) I've decided to keep it as local freehold slang for what happens when all the courts do their job to keep the Others out. But this Hedge write up was amazing. I loved Dave's kits and seemings, and court/freehold stuff, I love this hedge. I had a hard time shifting my group into the Hedge is Pain. But the laminar hedge that is and isn't is brilliant. That last preview alone gave me a lot of hope. Pile onto it the sooooo awesome stuff we've heard about the default but not default are and are not y splats...(the Seasonal Courts)...I think this will deliver in fairy tales and abuse metaphors both, but less focused on suffering. more confusion that can easily become suffering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T22:07:32-07:00","id":1077526,"title":"","content":"I'm 100% sympathetic to the reasons why the previous developer left, but looking only at the game design side, I didn't love most of the material that was previewed over the last couple years. I'm actually pretty excited to see a different take from another team!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T04:12:19-07:00","id":1077620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077301#post1077301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The former. <br /> <br /> Look, would it be helpful to people if I did a blog post and did a &amp;quot;how the sausage is made&amp;quot; on how a book goes from inception to publication? 'Cause there are a lot of little details and twists/turns that y'all don't know about (because why would you?) and they're important, but without context they'll sound...kind of thin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Include how things can change if the developer quits and I'm game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:54:18-07:00","id":1078485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077526#post1077526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm 100% sympathetic to the reasons why the previous developer left, but looking only at the game design side, I didn't love most of the material that was previewed over the last couple years. I'm actually pretty excited to see a different take from another team!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto! I'm sad David left under the circumstances he did, but his take on Changeling wasn't my cup of tea. Super excited to see what Rose will do with the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T13:34:10-07:00","id":1078505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1077515#post1077515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like open development, and this company can be great about it. I was there when Mummy was being talked about, and the end product represented what the developers and fans talked about. Some developers are more interactive than others, but so far, open development has always been fun, and always gets me excited for a product.<br /> <br /> While I was nervous about Bulwark being axed as a mechanic (if it has. I have a feeling its in the air, and its a tough decision and part of the open development process) I've decided to keep it as local freehold slang for what happens when all the courts do their job to keep the Others out. But this Hedge write up was amazing. I loved Dave's kits and seemings, and court/freehold stuff, I love this hedge. I had a hard time shifting my group into the Hedge is Pain. But the laminar hedge that is and isn't is brilliant. That last preview alone gave me a lot of hope. Pile onto it the sooooo awesome stuff we've heard about the default but not default are and are not y splats...(the Seasonal Courts)...I think this will deliver in fairy tales and abuse metaphors both, but less focused on suffering. more confusion that can easily become suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually have an idea how the old Hedge can be interested into the new Hedge, basically the idea is kind of like Wounds are in the Shadow, these places within the Hedge that have been corrupted by Ironside pain, places of mass murder, torture, horrific accidents, places frequently used for suicides, hospitals and prisons, all could cause local areas of the Hedge that are more the Hedge is Pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:28:07-07:00","id":1078624,"title":"","content":"While I read these foreign regularly, I rarely post anything. For a change of pace, I thought I'd throw in my two shekels...<br /> <br /> As a very Olde Skoole gamer (started in 1975), I learned early on that YMMV with any setting or system. WoD/NWoD/CoD have charged my imagination for many years. Of all the various lines in all the editions, C:tL has been, hands down, my favourite. I ran four campaigns and participated in two others, more than any of the other lines. As such, I have been both nervous and excited about the upcoming edition. The preview material has confirmed to me that a lot of care and love is being brought to bear with the update.<br /> <br /> Some people have complained that this or that hasn't been included or that some of the additions are out if step with what they want in the game. This is understandable; no game is perfect and no game survives its first meeting with th GM, much less the players. <br /> <br /> Personally, I am looking forward to the new edition. I intend, however, to mix it liberally with material from Ars Magica's Realms of Power: Faeries and touches of JAGS Wonderland. This doesn't mean I dislike the game, but rather that I find inspiration for my games from many sources. So, while I am saddened by the necessity of the change in the design team, due to what I had seen to date, I do recognize that necessity and place my trust in the crew now working on the project because they have, to date, shown great belief in and love for the line in general. <br /> <br /> In other words, once this Kicks, shut up and take my money! \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:24:56-07:00","id":1078657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MhicWombat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078624#post1078624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I read these foreign regularly, I rarely post anything. For a change of pace, I thought I'd throw in my two shekels...<br /> <br /> As a very Olde Skoole gamer (started in 1975), I learned early on that YMMV with any setting or system. WoD/NWoD/CoD have charged my imagination for many years. Of all the various lines in all the editions, C:tL has been, hands down, my favourite. I ran four campaigns and participated in two others, more than any of the other lines. As such, I have been both nervous and excited about the upcoming edition. The preview material has confirmed to me that a lot of care and love is being brought to bear with the update.<br /> <br /> Some people have complained that this or that hasn't been included or that some of the additions are out if step with what they want in the game. This is understandable; no game is perfect and no game survives its first meeting with th GM, much less the players. <br /> <br /> Personally, I am looking forward to the new edition. I intend, however, to mix it liberally with material from Ars Magica's Realms of Power: Faeries and touches of JAGS Wonderland. This doesn't mean I dislike the game, but rather that I find inspiration for my games from many sources. So, while I am saddened by the necessity of the change in the design team, due to what I had seen to date, I do recognize that necessity and place my trust in the crew now working on the project because they have, to date, shown great belief in and love for the line in general. <br /> <br /> In other words, once this Kicks, shut up and take my money! \ud83d\ude09</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually had an idea of making a certain section of Arcadia into different domains based on other settings/game systems, with the True Fae as a crazy DM.<br /> <br /> So one might be 5e forgotten realms, another Shadow Run, and so on, but when player visit them, the rules shiftto using that system for their duration of their stay, then shift based to regular CoD/Rules when they leave that domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T20:30:04-07:00","id":1078735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078505#post1078505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually have an idea how the old Hedge can be interested into the new Hedge, basically the idea is kind of like Wounds are in the Shadow, these places within the Hedge that have been corrupted by Ironside pain, places of mass murder, torture, horrific accidents, places frequently used for suicides, hospitals and prisons, all could cause local areas of the Hedge that are more the Hedge is Pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026The previous take on the Hedge was &quot;everything in the Hedge hurts <i>somebody</i>,&quot; not &quot;the entire Hedge is a field of pain.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was the Thicket Of Banes, not the Agony Zone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T22:35:21-07:00","id":1078769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078735#post1078735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026The previous take on the Hedge was &amp;quot;everything in the Hedge hurts <i>somebody</i>,&amp;quot; not &amp;quot;the entire Hedge is a field of pain.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> It was the Thicket Of Banes, not the Agony Zone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. The misrepresentation of David's presentation of the hedge had been bugging me, but I couldn't find the proper words to address it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T04:44:09-07:00","id":1078835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078735#post1078735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026The previous take on the Hedge was &amp;quot;everything in the Hedge hurts <i>somebody</i>,&amp;quot; not &amp;quot;the entire Hedge is a field of pain.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> It was the Thicket Of Banes, not the Agony Zone.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a good analogy, maybe not exactly as dark as. wounds, but still an areas where peoples pain kind accumulates, not all of which will be your pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:24:47-07:00","id":1078896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078735#post1078735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026The previous take on the Hedge was &quot;everything in the Hedge hurts <i>somebody</i>,&quot; not &quot;the entire Hedge is a field of pain.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was the Thicket Of Banes, not the Agony Zone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important point: It also edited itself to the feelings of the person(s) entering it. In other words, everything in it that was meant to hurt was either meant to hurt them, someone they cared about, or someone they hated. Everything there only existed to hurt someone <i>you</i> knew. Usually, you. It was not an impersonal thing that simply could be dangerous in a general sense; it homed in on your weaknesses and used them to stick you with razorblades, be they literal or metaphorical.<br /> <br /> The Hedge <i>was</i> the Agony Zone; a tailor-made place for you to find everything guaranteed to hurt <i>you</i>. Not in the general sense, but in the direct, laser-focused sense of <i>you</i>, personally. And as soon as it stopped being able to hurt? It disappeared.<br /> <br /> Hell, ArcaneArts outright said on this forum that the purpose of the Hedge is to hurt; that it doing so is what keeps the Gentry at bay because they don't like pain.<br /> <br /> The Hedge as something impersonal isn't in the text.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T09:03:17-07:00","id":1078909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078896#post1078896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important point: It also edited itself to the feelings of the person(s) entering it. In other words, everything in it that was meant to hurt was either meant to hurt them, someone they cared about, or someone they hated. <b>Everything there only existed to hurt someone <i>you</i> knew.</b> Usually, you. It was not an impersonal thing that simply could be dangerous in a general sense; <b>it homed in on your weaknesses and used them to stick you with razorblades,</b> be they literal or metaphorical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do not fucking lie to me about the contents of a publicly-available textual medium.<br /> <br /> It edited itself to specify that everything in it <i>had the capacity to hurt</i> and made a fairly extensive statement that some of that capacity-to-hurt was the pain of <i>getting it wrong</i> or <i>having to leave</i>.<br /> <br /> And &quot;the Hedge exists in-universe to cause pain&quot; was something that was only ever said <i>by you</i> or <i>in response to you</i>. The place was <i>built from</i> pain, but you may recall that it's also <i>where dreams lived</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hedge <i>was</i> the Agony Zone; a tailor-made place for you to find everything guaranteed to hurt <i>you</i>. Not in the general sense, but in the direct, laser-focused sense of <i>you</i>, personally. And as soon as it stopped being able to hurt? It disappeared. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyocUNHbEc0T1RQYVU/view\" target=\"_blank\">Go back and read it</a>, Axel, because I'm not doing this dance if you're going to deliberately ignore the steps for the sake of stomping on my feet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, ArcaneArts outright said on this forum that the purpose of the Hedge is to hurt; that it doing so is what keeps the Gentry at bay because they don't like pain. </div> </div> </div>You may recall that the Gentry's immunity to the hurting aspects of the Hedge was <i>also</i> stated, and &quot;Arc decided this&quot; was something that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974644#post974644\"><i>you made up</i></a>. Errol pointed this out the last time in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=976704#post976704\">a post you neglected to respond to</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hedge as something impersonal isn't in the text. </div> </div> </div>The Hedge as something honor-bound to personally ruin you and all you love is <i>also</i> not in the text. This is a textbook example of &quot;reader is making a special effort to be confused.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T09:25:57-07:00","id":1078920,"title":"","content":"In David-hedge, everything had the potential to hurt. That is very different from &quot;Everything there only existed to hurt someone <i>you</i> knew.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the difference between &quot;even something as beautiful as roses have thorns&quot; and &quot;literal hell&quot;... it's a very wide gap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T11:15:24-07:00","id":1078968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078909#post1078909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please do not fucking lie to me about the contents of a publicly-available textual medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a hell of an angry tone. I can understand if you're tired of people saying this stuff, but I resent being called a liar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078909#post1078909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It edited itself to specify that everything in it <i>had the capacity to hurt</i> and made a fairly extensive statement that some of that capacity-to-hurt was the pain of <i>getting it wrong</i> or <i>having to leave</i>.<br /> <br /> And &quot;the Hedge exists in-universe to cause pain&quot; was something that was only ever said <i>by you</i> or <i>in response to you</i>. The place was <i>built from</i> pain, but you may recall that it's also <i>where dreams lived</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like there's any sort of difference. I don't honestly care <i>how</i> something hurts you; I care that it does so <i>intentfully</i>. If you create a fantasy land full of wonders, just so you can strip it away and show the person who finally - <i>finally</i> - got to feel like a hero how illusory it all was, you still fucking hurt them. It doesn't matter if you didn't cut their body; you still cut their soul.<br /> <br /> Also, if something destroys any part of itself that doesn't at least hold the capacity to hurt someone? With no apparent connection to help people grow and change? That sounds like it exists to cause pain to me. Nothing about the Hedge is aspirational. Once something there loses its ability to hurt you, it vanishes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078909#post1078909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyocUNHbEc0T1RQYVU/view\" target=\"_blank\">Go back and read it</a>, Axel, because I'm not doing this dance if you're going to deliberately ignore the steps for the sake of stomping on my feet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with you, Satchel. This isn't some personal vendetta.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078909#post1078909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may recall that the Gentry's immunity to the hurting aspects of the Hedge was <i>also</i> stated, and &quot;Arc decided this&quot; was something that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974644#post974644\"><i>you made up</i></a>. Errol pointed this out the last time in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=976704#post976704\">a post you neglected to respond to</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973616#post973616\">Geeeet dunked on?</a><br /> <br /> Maybe actually read the thread next time before you call someone a liar, eh?<br /> <br /> Arcane never actually got back to me on that, something I don't blame them for; that thread got long. That's why I never bothered replying to Errol, either; I'd spent a few days defending my arguments there and was tired of the repetition. People disagreed with my perspective, which is fine; you don't have to feel the same way I do. I don't like the Hedge as a place that exists to cause pain - and it most certainly does; AA's response to Errol was to say that everything in the game was intended to distill down to &quot;pain&quot; - but people don't have to agree with me. They might see possibilities I don't.<br /> <br /> Also, the preview does note that the Gentry are immune to injury from the briars. Whether that means they simply aren't physically hampered, or whether that was changed after that post in a subsequent revision, I don't know. What I do know is that I was told that the design reason the Hedge exists is because the Gentry fear the pain it causes more than Changelings do, and I was told so by someone who wrote the section.<br /> <br /> Maybe that got changed, maybe that got edited, but I'm going to interpret it in that context until I hear otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078909#post1078909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hedge as something honor-bound to personally ruin you and all you love is <i>also</i> not in the text. This is a textbook example of &quot;reader is making a special effort to be confused.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a place literally made of hurt and pain. It is described as being akin to a dark alley coated with razor wire. &quot;What hurts you will always come back to hurt you and your loved ones again. That\u2019s the Hedge.&quot; The text states that everything there causes pain is a simplistic reading, and then goes on to use an example of how something you really want and enjoy can cause you pain; essentially implicating that it lures you in with good things and then makes you suffer for it; like the lure of a predatory fish. When you might expect some reward, some joy, some accomplishment for defanging it, it vanishes into faerie dust, because the Hedge ceases to embody something that hurts once it stops hurting.<br /> <br /> I don't think any of this is me reading what isn't there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T12:21:14-07:00","id":1078999,"title":"","content":"So, rather than trying to argue what David's pain Hedge was &quot;supposed to be&quot;, I'm just going to share something personal to explain why the pain Hedge spoke so strongly to me. People are free to take it or leave it as they please.<br /> <br /> I spent several years in a mutually abusive relationship. Neither of us realized what we were doing to each other at the time, but in retrospect, we were both absolutely horrible to each other. We are no longer a part of each other's lives at all, and for the better. Everything about that relationship was and is painful, and I couldn't get enough of it. Neither could they. We both took a kind of sick pride in being miserable together. And a part of me (a part I hate and am disgusted by) still does. Like that Halestorm song, &quot;I don't miss you, I miss the misery&quot;, part of me still hopes we'll reconnect some day and make each other's lives horrible, wonderful, passionate hell again. And that's what the pain-Hedge immediately made me think of. Yes, it hurts, but you don't fucking care because the pain is <i>exactly what makes it so wonderful</i>. It's not all repressed memories and psychological scars and personal degradation, any more than it's all barbed wire and rusty knives and razor blades. It's the smell of her purfume that still makes me feel that disgusting mix of hatred and longing. It's the dreams where I run into her at work and we catch up and realize we can be friends again, or maybe even more. It's the band she introduced me to still being my favorite musical artist. It's not the Pain Zone, it's <i>come on baby, make it hurt so good</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:10:13-07:00","id":1079036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078909#post1078909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Please do not fucking lie to me </b>about the contents of a publicly-available textual medium.<br /> <br /> The Hedge as something honor-bound to personally ruin you and all you love is <i>also</i> not in the text. <b>This is a textbook example of &quot;reader is making a special effort to be confused</b>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Not OK Satchel. I shouldn't have to tell you this. I don't want to issue a suspension but will if this tone continues.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T15:26:16-07:00","id":1079077,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> - Don't get me wrong; I understand why people would want that. If you like that, you do you. I just like a more broad toolbox to work with that allows for that, while also allowing for other stories too.<br /> <br /> A little while ago, I was talking with a friend about the changes - he doesn't check up on this stuff as religiously as I do - and he mentioned really liking the note about how, now, items lost in the Hedge may take on a life of their own; the sentiments attached to them growing (perhaps literal) roots. A Changeling taken as a child losing their teddy bear and it becoming a goblin.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, I just started stream-of-consciousnessing a story that might come from that. The Changeling character having this worrying propensity, when in the Hedge, of attracting nightmares. Not just nasty things but actual, literal nightmare-things; crept out of dreams and hunting for them. One day, when escaping one of these things, the Changeling's player fails a roll and stumbles. The nightmare chasing them is about to set upon the character when, out of the briars, comes launching an enormous beast. Chestnut brown fur periodically marked with stitches and scars and a terrible ursine growl follow as it savages the nightmare with all of its animal fury. The bear cannot kill the nightmare, but it drives it off; sending it scurrying back into the briars, tail between its hundreds of legs.<br /> <br /> The bear turns and looks at the Changeling. One eye missing, the wound sealed shut. The other dark and reflective, like a button. The bear turns and flees back into the briars after exchanging a long, silent, sad stare with the Lost one, who is left with the most uncanny sensation of just who that bear was.<br /> <br /> Cue adventures; sojourns into the Goblin Market or asking around at the freehold for who, if anyone, might know something about the bear. The Changeling wants the bear back by their side; to help keep away the terror. Eventually, after much bartering and trading, the Changeling sets out to a fabled Hollow in the Hedge; a place surrounded by thick briars, whose trods are stalked by nightmares, at the heart of which is a ruined (but still secure) castle. The Changeling - through whatever means - gets into the castle and finds its courtyard is full of doors that lead to nowhere. But as night falls, pathways appear within those doors; to bright, colourful, beautiful places. And that's when the bear returns.<br /> <br /> The Changeling explains why they're there but there isn't much time to talk. Nightmare beasts swarm the castle. Together, the Changeling and bear fend them off until morning.<br /> <br /> In the aftermath, the bear and the Changeling settle in. The bear can't speak, but it can nod and shake its head and the two can generally understand each other. The understandings come to the fore. The Changeling didn't mean to leave the bear behind; it was an accident. The bear can leave with them now. But the bear shakes its head sadly. It isn't angry. It's glad its former child is now all grown up and free from Arcadia. But its place is here; protecting the doorways to the dreams of children from nightmares. The Changeling understands. They let their precious childhood companion move on; passing it to the younger generation.<br /> <br /> They leave in the sunshine but, now and then, they return; having tea parties with the bear (with real tea this time), laughing, playing, and, come nightfall, donning armour and joining it in battle. Facing the nightmares, at last, rather than fleeing them. And pretty soon, the nightmare beasts no longer hunt the Changeling in the Hedge; afraid of the heroic figure who sends them fleeing into the dark.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I know this might feel a bit cutesy, but it's a fun little fairy tale to me. It's a story about growing up, and you could easily frame it against the act in the mundane world of, say, the Changeling suffering nightmares and going through their old things to look for a teddy bear, or going through things to pass off to a younger sibling, etc.<br /> <br /> It's a story with horror and fear and terror; of being chased and pursued by nightmares. But it's also a story of courage and bravery and learning to face the dark; of a character ultimately growing up and learning to put away childish things, yet at the same time achieving real maturity and being able to indulge them without needing them.<br /> <br /> It's a story that could have a lot of powerful emotions tied to the often disappointing sensation of growing up, and the pain of realizing that you can never really go back to carefree innocence; happiness stolen from you is gone forever. But it's also about maturing and coming to realize that so long as you're alive, you can be happy for what you had and find new happiness; new ways to grow and become better than before.<br /> <br /> If this were the other Hedge, the agony wall, the bear and the castle would cease to be as soon as the Changeling came to terms with the fact that they can't have what they used to have anymore. Once they made peace, it'd cease to be; an act which would lead to the whole thing being tinged with loss, rather than a contented acceptance.<br /> <br /> I like hope in my stories. Darkness and terror are great, but if that's all it is, it's just exhausting. I like happy endings. I like the hero's efforts to be worth it.<br /> <br /> I don't figure this is for everyone, but I like beauty in my beautiful madness, and I like fairy tales. That's why I play Changeling. If it's not for you... Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T15:36:39-07:00","id":1079084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078999#post1078999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, rather than trying to argue what David's pain Hedge was &amp;quot;supposed to be&amp;quot;, I'm just going to share something personal to explain why the pain Hedge spoke so strongly to me. People are free to take it or leave it as they please.<br /> <br /> I spent several years in a mutually abusive relationship. Neither of us realized what we were doing to each other at the time, but in retrospect, we were both absolutely horrible to each other. We are no longer a part of each other's lives at all, and for the better. Everything about that relationship was and is painful, and I couldn't get enough of it. Neither could they. We both took a kind of sick pride in being miserable together. And a part of me (a part I hate and am disgusted by) still does. Like that Halestorm song, &amp;quot;I don't miss you, I miss the misery&amp;quot;, part of me still hopes we'll reconnect some day and make each other's lives horrible, wonderful, passionate hell again. And that's what the pain-Hedge immediately made me think of. Yes, it hurts, but you don't fucking care because the pain is <i>exactly what makes it so wonderful</i>. It's not all repressed memories and psychological scars and personal degradation, any more than it's all barbed wire and rusty knives and razor blades. It's the smell of her purfume that still makes me feel that disgusting mix of hatred and longing. It's the dreams where I run into her at work and we catch up and realize we can be friends again, or maybe even more. It's the band she introduced me to still being my favorite musical artist. It's not the Pain Zone, it's <i>come on baby, make it hurt so good</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's fucking awesome, its disturbingly beautiful, emotional sadomasochism for lack if a better word contained in a relationship. <br /> <br /> I totally get it, but in a different way, for me it's a sexually fantasy that doesn't just turn me on, it makes me so fucking disgusted with myself that I can't help but wonder if I should be put down, but yet that guilt makes it ten times hotter. <br /> <br /> Of course I've since learned fantasies aren't evil, because evil is an action, and I've slowly learned that my sexual sadism doesn't make me a monster, as long as I indulge it consentually or in my own mind, it's not immoral, I have conscience and I use it. <br /> <br /> Still sometimes the toxic mix of taboo thrill, self loathing, and lust can be intoxicating. <br /> <br /> But I'd never trade that in for self acceptance and inner peace that I've gained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:10:06-07:00","id":1079101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079077#post1079077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> - Don't get me wrong; I understand why people would want that. If you like that, you do you. I just like a more broad toolbox to work with that allows for that, while also allowing for other stories too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that's a reasonable critique of the pain-Hedge. It's also a World of difference from hyperbolically characterizing the pain-Hedge as nothing but doom and gloom and misery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079077#post1079077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A little while ago, I was talking with a friend about the changes - he doesn't check up on this stuff as religiously as I do - and he mentioned really liking the note about how, now, items lost in the Hedge may take on a life of their own; the sentiments attached to them growing (perhaps literal) roots. A Changeling taken as a child losing their teddy bear and it becoming a goblin.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, I just started stream-of-consciousnessing a story that might come from that. The Changeling character having this worrying propensity, when in the Hedge, of attracting nightmares. Not just nasty things but actual, literal nightmare-things; crept out of dreams and hunting for them. One day, when escaping one of these things, the Changeling's player fails a roll and stumbles. The nightmare chasing them is about to set upon the character when, out of the briars, comes launching an enormous beast. Chestnut brown fur periodically marked with stitches and scars and a terrible ursine growl follow as it savages the nightmare with all of its animal fury. The bear cannot kill the nightmare, but it drives it off; sending it scurrying back into the briars, tail between its hundreds of legs.<br /> <br /> The bear turns and looks at the Changeling. One eye missing, the wound sealed shut. The other dark and reflective, like a button. The bear turns and flees back into the briars after exchanging a long, silent, sad stare with the Lost one, who is left with the most uncanny sensation of just who that bear was.<br /> <br /> Cue adventures; sojourns into the Goblin Market or asking around at the freehold for who, if anyone, might know something about the bear. The Changeling wants the bear back by their side; to help keep away the terror. Eventually, after much bartering and trading, the Changeling sets out to a fabled Hollow in the Hedge; a place surrounded by thick briars, whose trods are stalked by nightmares, at the heart of which is a ruined (but still secure) castle. The Changeling - through whatever means - gets into the castle and finds its courtyard is full of doors that lead to nowhere. But as night falls, pathways appear within those doors; to bright, colourful, beautiful places. And that's when the bear returns.<br /> <br /> The Changeling explains why they're there but there isn't much time to talk. Nightmare beasts swarm the castle. Together, the Changeling and bear fend them off until morning.<br /> <br /> In the aftermath, the bear and the Changeling settle in. The bear can't speak, but it can nod and shake its head and the two can generally understand each other. The understandings come to the fore. The Changeling didn't mean to leave the bear behind; it was an accident. The bear can leave with them now. But the bear shakes its head sadly. It isn't angry. It's glad its former child is now all grown up and free from Arcadia. But its place is here; protecting the doorways to the dreams of children from nightmares. The Changeling understands. They let their precious childhood companion move on; passing it to the younger generation.<br /> <br /> They leave in the sunshine but, now and then, they return; having tea parties with the bear (with real tea this time), laughing, playing, and, come nightfall, donning armour and joining it in battle. Facing the nightmares, at last, rather than fleeing them. And pretty soon, the nightmare beasts no longer hunt the Changeling in the Hedge; afraid of the heroic figure who sends them fleeing into the dark.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I know this might feel a bit cutesy, but it's a fun little fairy tale to me. It's a story about growing up, and you could easily frame it against the act in the mundane world of, say, the Changeling suffering nightmares and going through their old things to look for a teddy bear, or going through things to pass off to a younger sibling, etc.<br /> <br /> It's a story with horror and fear and terror; of being chased and pursued by nightmares. But it's also a story of courage and bravery and learning to face the dark; of a character ultimately growing up and learning to put away childish things, yet at the same time achieving real maturity and being able to indulge them without needing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a very cool story. It doesn't strike me as very Lost, though. Stories about growing up and learning to put away childish things are more Dreaming's wheelhouse, from what I understand. Not that Lost can't be used to tell them, but they're certainly not what <i>I</i> go to Lost for. (And in case it needed saying, it's fine if we take different meaning from the game. Just sharing my own perspective, not shaming yours.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079077#post1079077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a story that could have a lot of powerful emotions tied to the often disappointing sensation of growing up, and the pain of realizing that you can never really go back to carefree innocence; happiness stolen from you is gone forever. But it's also about maturing and coming to realize that so long as you're alive, you can be happy for what you had and find new happiness; new ways to grow and become better than before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could work with that. Emphasizing the bittersweetness of loss of innocence brings it a little more into Lost territory for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079077#post1079077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this were the other Hedge, the agony wall, the bear and the castle would cease to be as soon as the Changeling came to terms with the fact that they can't have what they used to have anymore. Once they made peace, it'd cease to be; an act which would lead to the whole thing being tinged with loss, rather than a contented acceptance.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this strikes me as too simplistic of a way of looking at it. It treats coming to terms with that loss of childhood and making peace as a thing you do once and then it's finished. But to me at least, that's not how life or coping with loss work. It's something you always strive for. Something you have to remind yourself of every day. The Bear doesn't disappear from the hedge because you don't just stop missing those childhood things, and missing them doesn't just stop stinging. The happiness you take from learning to move on is real, and you take that with you for ever, but it doesn't erase the pain, nor the pain the happiness.<br /> <br /> <i>I do need you, Hoggle. Every now and again in my life, for no reason at all, I need you. All of you.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079077#post1079077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like hope in my stories. Darkness and terror are great, but if that's all it is, it's just exhausting. I like happy endings. I like the hero's efforts to be worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this we agree, and it's because of this that I have a negative reaction to seeing the pain-Hedge being talked about like it's nothing but unending torment and woe. I like hope in my games too, but hope is a bittersweet thing. I like happy endings as a thing to strive for, but I also firmly believe in the addage that there are no happy endings because there are no endings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079077#post1079077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't figure this is for everyone, but I like beauty in my beautiful madness, and I like fairy tales. That's why I play Changeling. If it's not for you... Fair enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the beauty as well (though I preferred &quot;beautiful lies and bittersweet truths&quot; over &quot;beautiful madness&quot;) but I don't think the pain-Hedge diminished that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's all moot now. The pain-Hedge is not canon any more, which is a shame in my opinion but what can you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-15-2017, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:22:12-07:00","id":1079106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079084#post1079084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's fucking awesome, its disturbingly beautiful, emotional sadomasochism for lack if a better word contained in a relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand you mean well by saying this, but I'd prefer you didn't. I'm not proud of what I did to her, and while I'll probably never completely be rid of the pride I have for surviving what she did to me, it's not a feeling I like having. I have to live with knowing that I was an abuser and I would rather that not be glorified. That kind of dynamic is glorified enough in popular media, between the songs I referenced, countless others with similar themes, and as many examples of similar toxic relationships in movies, books, and TV being presented as desirable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:23:27-07:00","id":1079107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078999#post1078999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, rather than trying to argue what David's pain Hedge was &quot;supposed to be&quot;, I'm just going to share something personal to explain why the pain Hedge spoke so strongly to me. People are free to take it or leave it as they please.<br /> <br /> I spent several years in a mutually abusive relationship. Neither of us realized what we were doing to each other at the time, but in retrospect, we were both absolutely horrible to each other. We are no longer a part of each other's lives at all, and for the better. Everything about that relationship was and is painful, and I couldn't get enough of it. Neither could they. We both took a kind of sick pride in being miserable together. And a part of me (a part I hate and am disgusted by) still does. Like that Halestorm song, &quot;I don't miss you, I miss the misery&quot;, part of me still hopes we'll reconnect some day and make each other's lives horrible, wonderful, passionate hell again. And that's what the pain-Hedge immediately made me think of. Yes, it hurts, but you don't fucking care because the pain is <i>exactly what makes it so wonderful</i>. It's not all repressed memories and psychological scars and personal degradation, any more than it's all barbed wire and rusty knives and razor blades. It's the smell of her purfume that still makes me feel that disgusting mix of hatred and longing. It's the dreams where I run into her at work and we catch up and realize we can be friends again, or maybe even more. It's the band she introduced me to still being my favorite musical artist. It's not the Pain Zone, it's <i>come on baby, make it hurt so good</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this interpretation of it alot - sorry to hear about the relationship but great example - I feel very much the same way in terms of the ideology of the Hedge <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:27:25-07:00","id":1079109,"title":"","content":"I don't say this to be accusatory or combative, but it feels very strange to say that while having an avatar of one of the most fetishized abuse victims in popular culture today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:34:06-07:00","id":1079113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079109#post1079109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't say this to be accusatory or combative, but it feels very strange to say that while having an avatar of one of the most fetishized abuse victims in popular culture today.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense taken. I have pretty mixed feelings about Harley, for that reason among others, and I resisted using her for an avatar despite the obvious connection to my username for... how many years, now? Five? Ultimately I decided I was ok with it only if I used a depiction of her from the animated series, my favorite version of the character, and one where her abuse is distinctly not presented in a positive light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:39:51-07:00","id":1079114,"title":"","content":"This is true. That series did it more justice than most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T17:02:17-07:00","id":1079119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079106#post1079106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand you mean well by saying this, but I'd prefer you didn't. I'm not proud of what I did to her, and while I'll probably never completely be rid of the pride I have for surviving what she did to me, it's not a feeling I like having. I have to live with knowing that I was an abuser and I would rather that not be glorified. That kind of dynamic is glorified enough in popular media, between the songs I referenced, countless others with similar themes, and as many examples of similar toxic relationships in movies, books, and TV being presented as desirable.</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess the difference is I never actually did anything bad to anyone, a thought is not an action, a consenting roleplay not the same as actually being hurtful, so that makes it different form you experiences. <br /> <br /> I hope some day you can forgive yourself and her and heal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T19:25:56-07:00","id":1079173,"title":"","content":"Well, since I'm being invoked, I may as well chime in pointlessly again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078968#post1078968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcane never actually got back to me on that, something I don't blame them for; that thread got long. That's why I never bothered replying to Errol, either; I'd spent a few days defending my arguments there and was tired of the repetition. People disagreed with my perspective, which is fine; you don't have to feel the same way I do. I don't like the Hedge as a place that exists to cause pain - and it most certainly does; AA's response to Errol was to say that everything in the game was intended to distill down to &quot;pain&quot; - but people don't have to agree with me. They might see possibilities I don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you have a narrow interpretation of pain, and what you can do with it story-wise. In my view, <i>everything</i> is pain. How something hurts is a perspective through which you can look at literally anything. So when someone says, &quot;This is about pain,&quot; to me that's just saying, &quot;I'm choosing to use this frame of reference.&quot; It is not the only perspective that exists, but it is <i>a</i> perspective and it's a valid one to have.<br /> <br /> I can't point to a single experience in my life that doesn't hurt. To me, life is about choosing what kind of pain I experience, what cost I'm willing to pay in order to have something I want. Or, y'know, <i>not</i> having that choice, since life does not care about your wants.<br /> <br /> The idea that your Changeling, going back into the Hedge to have tea with the Bear, isn't feeling some measure of pain really doesn't make sense to me. But perhaps more importantly, the idea that the Hedge exists <i>only</i> as a description of outsiders' pains doesn't make sense to me. Once something has hurt once, and it manifests in the Hedge, it takes on a life of its own. To take the most absurd example, if you get a paper cut and it stings and that manifests in the Hedge as a paper mosquito flitting around, it doesn't just... vanish when the cut heals. I'd expect it to stick around and join the Hedge ecology being a paper mosquito doing paper mosquito things. So why would the Bear and the castle vanish? What requires that?<br /> <br /> To make an analogy, in the Shadow, spirits don't die when the essence that awoke them stops showing up. That's the entire reason there's a bunch of spirits who flit around doing stuff unrelated to how they were originally manifested. I don't see any reason why the same kind of thing isn't true of the Hedge. The difference is mainly that, in the Hedge, it's much more obvious and in-your-face where a goblin came from... if it's part of your story. But something like a goblin market doesn't make sense as something that'd exist if Hedge denizens only existed at the sufferance of some specific pain that someone is presently experiencing. Hell, nothing in the Hedge could possibly exist for longer than particular lifespans.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the only reason the Bear and castle <i>should</i> vanish is precisely to signify that the Changeling <i>has</i> put away childish things, as you put it, and grown up and is no longer indulging. You could get very Susan Pevensie about it and say that Arcadia doesn't really exist and it was very fun to play king and queen but now I have lipstick and dresses. But, in your telling, the Bear and the castle are <i>not</i> childish things. And acknowledging that things that hurt you don't magically disappear once you've moved on--that just because you know kung fu doesn't actually mean Smith is going to stop coming for you--is also part of growing up. In seeking a happy ending, I honestly feel like you've made a fairly bittersweet one.<br /> <br /> Anyways. It's not like this is a relevant thing to be arguing about anymore.<br /> <br /> Which kinda hurts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T19:36:53-07:00","id":1079178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079119#post1079119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I hope some day you can forgive yourself and her and heal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I have forgiven her - we were young and stupid and didn't know any better and I don't hold that against her. It's not my place to forgive myself. The best I can to is to understand and acknowledge what I did wrong, and to learn from that and be a better person going forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T19:38:41-07:00","id":1079180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079113#post1079113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No offense taken. I have pretty mixed feelings about Harley, for that reason among others, and I resisted using her for an avatar despite the obvious connection to my username for... how many years, now? Five? Ultimately I decided I was ok with it only if I used a depiction of her from the animated series, my favorite version of the character, and one where her abuse is distinctly not presented in a positive light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here here. It doesn't help that Harley is being sexualized in her later iterations, along with presenting the abuse as anything but. I know it's not exactly new, but what about Harley in her new costumes are anything close to a harlequin? There no practical purpose to it, outside of showing off skin. Her original outfit may be skin tight but at least it offered some meager protection from various things. And why make her a killer of children when she was about love and fun?<br /> <br /> Sorry, diatribe here that isn't needed.<br /> <br /> Is it wrong for me to want to make Harley a Changeling? A Wizened possibly, using her slapstick, athleticism and chaotic intellect to escape the mortal danger of her realm? Or would an Elemental work better, given she can look back on her chaos and make a grand picture about it and her place in life...or a mess that knocks off some of her clarity?<br /> <br /> Also, Charlaquin, I'm sorry that you went through such a troubled part of your life as you did. Normally guilty pleasures aren't depicted as being bad, but that's one of the darkest ones I've read about. I'm glad that you've managed to not only recognize how unhealthy it was but to end it, move on, and forgive the other side for their part in it. Great respect to you for that - I've seen people do far less in lesser situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-15-2017, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T19:58:04-07:00","id":1079188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079180#post1079180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong for me to want to make Harley a Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>She fits the metaphor. So the Joker would be her Keeper, I take it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079180#post1079180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Wizened possibly, using her slapstick, athleticism and chaotic intellect to escape the mortal danger of her realm? Or would an Elemental work better, given she can look back on her chaos and make a grand picture about it and her place in life...or a mess that knocks off some of her clarity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say under David's paradaigm of Seemings (who knows if that'll change or not), I think Elemental is probably the best fit. What's her element though? Comedy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079180#post1079180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Charlaquin, I'm sorry that you went through such a troubled part of your life as you did. Normally guilty pleasures aren't depicted as being bad, but that's one of the darkest ones I've read about. I'm glad that you've managed to not only recognize how unhealthy it was but to end it, move on, and forgive the other side for their part in it. Great respect to you for that - I've seen people do far less in lesser situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I hope I haven't completely derailed the thread by bringing it up. I think at this point I'm going to say that if anyone wants to discuss it further they're welcome to do so via PM, but otherwise we should bring the discussion back to Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T20:16:36-07:00","id":1079196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079188#post1079188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She fits the metaphor. So the Joker would be her Keeper, I take it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Batman - in normal media he has a habit of helping create his own villains, or attracting them to himself. As a True Fae he'd be the force of the night that always cracks down on crime, avenging mythical figures only he's aware of, the ultimate detective who is addicted to solving crime, and thus must make those who would cause it. The Joker would have just been another Changeling, possibly one Harley had been familiar with before her durance, hence her familiarity and loyalty to him. Mister J is too obsessed to leave his Keeper though - Harley got out when she realized she was getting the same way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079188#post1079188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say under David's paradaigm of Seemings (who knows if that'll change or not), I think Elemental is probably the best fit. What's her element though? Comedy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, fair point, I'd forgotten that. If the Seemings stay the same, I'd say her Element is actually closer to Timing/Time - knowing when to move, how much suspense is needed for a joke, or even how long to set a bomb is all needed, particularly for an escape from a realm like Gotham. Reflexes that extend past normal senses, and into the very flow of the moment, however strange that flow is. Plus, Harley seems stuck in time in a way - she can't move past that time with Mister J, the Batman, always falling back into bad habits when time has proven their destructiveness. She utilizes that destruction even as it works at her, even if she keeps smiling.<br /> <br /> That said, comedy is a pretty good means too, particularly for something like Cloak Of The Elements - pratfalls, various things emerging from one's sleeve, electric joy buzzers, all kinds of things that a harlequin could use to both delight and devastate with. Comedy she can both utilize...and fall victim to as well, though she has some level of immunity to it that keeps it funny rather than cringe-worthy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079188#post1079188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. I hope I haven't completely derailed the thread by bringing it up. I think at this point I'm going to say that if anyone wants to discuss it further they're welcome to do so via PM, but otherwise we should bring the discussion back to Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>No derailing at all. It was a very pertinent analogy, if a personal one, and it actually gives a bit of relatability to the otherwise completely alien force of narrative at play. Thank you for sharing that part of yourself Charlaquin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-15-2017, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T20:29:43-07:00","id":1079202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079196#post1079196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Batman - in normal media he has a habit of helping create his own villains, or attracting them to himself. As a True Fae he'd be the force of the night that always cracks down on crime, avenging mythical figures only he's aware of, the ultimate detective who is addicted to solving crime, and thus must make those who would cause it. The Joker would have just been another Changeling, possibly one Harley had been familiar with before her durance, hence her familiarity and loyalty to him. Mister J is too obsessed to leave his Keeper though - Harley got out when she realized she was getting the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, damn, that's a really cool take! So, then, might she actually be a Fairest to Joker's Darkling? I guess she doesn't have the leadership angle, and Elemental's Blessing and Curse fit her really well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T20:36:49-07:00","id":1079205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079173#post1079173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that you have a narrow interpretation of pain, and what you can do with it story-wise. In my view, <i>everything</i> is pain. How something hurts is a perspective through which you can look at literally anything. So when someone says, &quot;This is about pain,&quot; to me that's just saying, &quot;I'm choosing to use this frame of reference.&quot; It is not the only perspective that exists, but it is <i>a</i> perspective and it's a valid one to have.<br /> <br /> I can't point to a single experience in my life that doesn't hurt. To me, life is about choosing what kind of pain I experience, what cost I'm willing to pay in order to have something I want. Or, y'know, <i>not</i> having that choice, since life does not care about your wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say your definition of pain is overly broad. If everything is pain, why talk about something causing pain at all? It will follow as a natural consequence. Why talk about things disappearing when they cease to cause pain if they always can and will?<br /> <br /> You're free to have your own perspective, and all, but whatever ideas you may possess differ wildly and markedly than the ones that went into the text. The authors clearly have a meaning for pain beyond &quot;Every aspect of human experience&quot;. It is specifically an agonized sensation that somethings cause or can cause, and some things do not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079173#post1079173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that your Changeling, going back into the Hedge to have tea with the Bear, isn't feeling some measure of pain really doesn't make sense to me. But perhaps more importantly, the idea that the Hedge exists <i>only</i> as a description of outsiders' pains doesn't make sense to me. Once something has hurt once, and it manifests in the Hedge, it takes on a life of its own. To take the most absurd example, if you get a paper cut and it stings and that manifests in the Hedge as a paper mosquito flitting around, it doesn't just... vanish when the cut heals. I'd expect it to stick around and join the Hedge ecology being a paper mosquito doing paper mosquito things. So why would the Bear and the castle vanish? What requires that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The preview document. The preview document requires that. And I quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of it could hurt. And if it starts hurting, it goes away once it stops hurting. </div> </div> </div>So once the Changeling feels the pain of being unable to reclaim their youthful innocence, then comes to terms with it and matures and accepts that they need to move forward, not try to capture the past? Bear goes bye-bye. The rose withers without its thorns; the sword with a dulled edge fades to dust.<br /> <br /> Now, if you take the overly broad interpretation of pain that you have and apply it, sure, it'd persist then, because it could <i>theoretically</i> hurt them again, but if you take an interpretation that broad, there's literally nothing that would ever disappear. Cut the thorns off a rose? It'll still fucking hurt if I jam the stem in your eye. Just got the petals? Well, I could still force them down your throat and choke you, so I guess they can stay! Et cetera.<br /> <br /> But I get the feeling that wasn't what the authors intended. Once the thing that hurt you can't hurt you anymore, it disappears.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079173#post1079173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically, the only reason the Bear and castle <i>should</i> vanish is precisely to signify that the Changeling <i>has</i> put away childish things, as you put it, and grown up and is no longer indulging. You could get very Susan Pevensie about it and say that Arcadia doesn't really exist and it was very fun to play king and queen but now I have lipstick and dresses. But, in your telling, the Bear and the castle are <i>not</i> childish things. And acknowledging that things that hurt you don't magically disappear once you've moved on--that just because you know kung fu doesn't actually mean Smith is going to stop coming for you--is also part of growing up. In seeking a happy ending, I honestly feel like you've made a fairly bittersweet one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Call it what you like. I like it better than Bear just ceasing to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T20:41:48-07:00","id":1079207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079202#post1079202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, damn, that's a really cool take! So, then, might she actually be a Fairest to Joker's Darkling? I guess she doesn't have the leadership angle, and Elemental's Blessing and Curse fit her really well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I pondered a Fairest, but as written right now they're natural leaders, and Harley is typically a follower. She can and has done great things when she's struck out on her own, and her plans are proven to be more reliable than Jokers, but any authority tends to get her to follow their ways. That's actually why I went with Wizened at first, since they strive to be the best they can be in their craft - Harley strives to be the best she can to earn the love of Joker (which naturally is not a happy direction to go in) and that involves doing her job, which she has proven to be pretty dang capable of...when the slapstick bug doesn't bite anyways.<br /> <br /> Joker as a Darkling fits to a T though, and a few other letters for good measure. Edit: Actually, Joker almost fits Fairest better than Darkling. He's amazing at what he does, he's never low on minions, and he has that charisma that either gets you doing what he wants or gets under your skin...and hey, he can take a beating and still look good, if the Mark Hamill version is anything to go by. That said, he doesn't seem to worry about those under him getting hurt, so that's the Fairest curse out the window...or maybe Wizened, with his sanity being what went out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-15-2017, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T20:45:47-07:00","id":1079208,"title":"","content":"Harley seems like an Orger, a lot of violence there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T21:19:16-07:00","id":1079216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079205#post1079205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I get the feeling that wasn't what the authors intended. Once the thing that hurt you can't hurt you anymore, it disappears.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet at the same time, places cease to exist when <i>truly forgotten</i>. Pain-Hedge-landscape explicitly includes archetypal features of the local human experience \u2014 do you imagine that the authors intended the Mona Lisa to exude agony? Pain-Hedge landscape was where we saw the introduction of deliberate mortal Hedge-shaping \u2014 this is not a thing that makes sense if the Hedge literally and totally only exists for the sake of inflicting pain, particularly given that using shaping to form weapons and other explicitly painful things gets no special treatment from the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Life is suffering and caring about things makes you vulnerable to their manipulation and/or manipulations. This is not news, but it is relevant, in Changeling as in the rest of the Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Ghosts persist on the force of memory and the passion \u2014 a word derived from a Latin root meaning &quot;to suffer&quot; \u2014 that compels them to dwell among those recollections, and they frequently vanish beyond knowability when their needs are fulfilled because that's all that keeping them anything like alive.<br /> <br /> Werewolves send spirits back to the Shadow because those entities fuck a body up forcing it to focus on transient aspects of reality so the invisible monster hooked onto their flesh can eat.<br /> <br /> Mages regularly aspire to a state of pure symbolic existence that doesn't have to worry about the complications of time and space and life.<br /> <br /> Mummies literally have a mythology in which suffering is the foundation of the persistent universe, made worthwhile by the ability to move through suffering.<br /> <br /> Beasts overwhelmingly feed on varying levels of suffering and are incentivized by their nature to improve their ability to survive one or more types of pain because the closest thing they have to the luxury of lasting satisfaction is to kill their humanity and exist as an idea roving throughout the basement of the mortal fundament.<br /> <br /> The Fae primarily dwell in palaces and fields where the very forces of destiny conspire to give them what they want or need save for when that would interfere with the various assented-to levels of conflict that they agreed to in order to exist with a semidistinct identity.<br /> <br /> Changelings carry the joys and terrors of their Durance with them for the rest of their lives and maybe further still. They do the same for their mortal lives and their lives among the Lost, and they're the most readily-competent at shaping the Hedge.<br /> <br /> The entire extended setting overflows with examples of how mortal-adjacent supernatural forces have a tendency to cling to things they should allow to pass and how the worlds outside the material realm are frequently more open about hidden aspects of the world of skin and flesh. The Hedge as a place of pain where dreams and Hollows offer a brief respite was not unprecedented, but that doesn't make it the central, defining, overriding point of the place any more than 1e Geist's take on the Underworld as a place that showcases sin makes every errant specter in the place a degenerate hedonist or Werewolf's take on the Shadow as a place of hungry spirits makes any scene there that's not a banquet or a fight over scraps ring false.<br /> <br /> The Pain-Hedge was a place where the bare-bones fundamental reason for most activities within it to be occurring was to make someone or something hurt more or less than it did, with the understanding that, outside the depths of true timelessness and endless sleep that one might find in distant Arcadia, these changes would be wildly-varying levels of temporary and sometimes might be little more than the fleeting comfort of schadenfreude. That didn't stop you from having meaningful growth stem from the journey or the settlement, because, again, caring about something in the Hedge inherently gives it an excuse to keep existing one way or the other until something else gobbles it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T22:21:38-07:00","id":1079237,"title":"","content":"I dunno, but I feel as if this quote from the Dresden Files feels as if it fits in this thread, for some reason:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jim Butcher</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cSure, we'd faced some things as children that a lot of kids don't. Sure, Justin had qualified for his Junior de Sade Badge in his teaching methods for dealing with pain. We still hadn't learned, though, that growing up is all about getting hurt. And then getting over it. You hurt. You recover. You move on. Odds are pretty good you're just going to get hurt again. But each time, you learn something.<br /> <br /> Each time, you come out of it a little stronger, and at some point you realize that there are more flavors of pain than coffee. There's the little empty pain of leaving something behind - gradutaing, taking the next step forward, walking out of something familiar and safe into the unknown. There's the big, whirling pain of life upending all of your plans and expecations. There's the sharp little pains of failure, and the more obscure aches of successes that didn't give you what you thought they would. There are the vicious, stabbing pains of hopes being torn up. The sweet little pains of finding others, giving them your love, and taking joy in their life they grow and learn. There's the steady pain of empathy that you shrug off so you can stand beside a wounded friend and help them bear their burdens.<br /> <br /> And if you're very, very lucky, there are a very few blazing hot little pains you feel when you realized that you are standing in a moment of utter perfection, an instant of triumph, or happiness, or mirth which at the same time cannot possibly last - and yet will remain with you for life.<br /> <br /> Everyone is down on pain, because they forget something important about it: Pain is for the living. Only the dead don't feel it.<br /> <br /> Pain is a part of life. Sometimes it's a big part, and sometimes it isn't, but either way, it's a part of the big puzzle, the deep music, the great game. Pain does two things: It teaches you, tells you that you're alive. Then it passes away and leaves you changed. It leaves you wiser, sometimes. Sometimes it leaves you stronger. Either way, pain leaves its mark, and everything important that will ever happen to you in life is going to involve it in one degree or another.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T00:49:18-07:00","id":1079282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1078896#post1078896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, ArcaneArts outright said on this forum that the purpose of the Hedge is to hurt; that it doing so is what keeps the Gentry at bay because they don't like pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to invoke me, make sure you understand <i>my</i> point of view on pain-namely, that <i>pain is precious. </i>Otherwise, kindly don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T01:14:44-07:00","id":1079291,"title":"","content":"I apologize if I misrepresented you in some way. If you want, though, you could end all of this tedious debate right here by clarifying it.<br /> <br /> Does the Hedge exist to cause pain? Was that its central thesis in your write-up?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T03:05:27-07:00","id":1079309,"title":"","content":"From perspective of time, I feel Dave Hill's forum posts made a much better job of explaining the Hedge than his playtest materials did. The draft carried a strong concept and David described it in an impressionistic manner. However, when many people read an RPG book they expect a manual instead of a poem. Not everyone immerses themselves in nuances of language. If they're told that the Hedge causes pain, they will take it for granted rather that extending the definition of pain to all of human existence. The fact that multiple bright people are still arguing about that should act as evidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T06:27:03-07:00","id":1079346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079282#post1079282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to invoke me, make sure you understand <i>my</i> point of view on pain-namely, that <i>pain is precious. </i>Otherwise, kindly don't.</div> </div> </div> </div> That reminded me of Captain Kirk in the movie Star Trek: The Final Frontier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T11:30:25-07:00","id":1079446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079291#post1079291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if I misrepresented you in some way. If you want, though, you could end all of this tedious debate right here by clarifying it.<br /> <br /> Does the Hedge exist to cause pain? Was that its central thesis in your write-up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't write it, though the writer definitely agreed with my point, so I will clarify my point after I do my morning routine.<br /> <br /> One thing I wanna get out now as a side note is that, due to a lot of the baggage around these threads, I've been trying to avoid getting involved so as to avoid stressing a tense situation even more-I found out about my invocation through a friend. You didn't know that, so no worries, but some of my annoyance comes from that. So, you know. Here's the heads up to everyone about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-16-2017, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T11:48:31-07:00","id":1079453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079309#post1079309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From perspective of time, I feel Dave Hill's forum posts made a much better job of explaining the Hedge than his playtest materials did. The draft carried a strong concept and David described it in an impressionistic manner. However, when many people read an RPG book they expect a manual instead of a poem. Not everyone immerses themselves in nuances of language. If they're told that the Hedge causes pain, they will take it for granted rather that extending the definition of pain to all of human existence. The fact that multiple bright people are still arguing about that should act as evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong. Its a difficult thing to balance between nuance for those who appreciate it and straightforwardness for those who need it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T17:48:55-07:00","id":1079587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079446#post1079446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't write it, though the writer definitely agreed with my point, so I will clarify my point after I do my morning routine.<br /> <br /> One thing I wanna get out now as a side note is that, due to a lot of the baggage around these threads, I've been trying to avoid getting involved so as to avoid stressing a tense situation even more-I found out about my invocation through a friend. You didn't know that, so no worries, but some of my annoyance comes from that. So, you know. Here's the heads up to everyone about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, mate. That's your prerogative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:07:19-07:00","id":1079625,"title":"","content":"Setting aside the prose for a second to look at the mechanics of the place, David's version of the Hedge typically dealt one bashing per hour. And that's if you were off the path, trying to travel at some speed. That's... not that much of a deterrent. It's not any worse than trying to push through moderately difficult undergrowth ironsides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T07:08:19-07:00","id":1079777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079453#post1079453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not wrong. Its a difficult thing to balance between nuance for those who appreciate it and straightforwardness for those who need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, this is one of the central problems of creating setting-heavy RPG books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A related problem is how much space to devote to examples versus general description. Too much description, and you're telling not showing. Too many examples, and you're not providing enough framework to create new examples of the setting element. nWoD 1e started out way too light on examples, and that got it a lot of criticism (both deserved and not) for being flavorless and lacking detail. In 2e, we've gone much heavier on examples: my guideline is that every time we describe a general phenomenon, we give one to three specific instances of it.<br /> <br /> (I'm specifically thinking of the covenants from VtR2, where in 1e I was consistently asked &quot;but what do they <i>do</i>?,&quot; but it's on my mind right now due to the discussion on the Hedge preview I posted last week, which was the example part rather than the framework part.)<br /> <br /> I think one of the reasons <i>Changeling</i> 1e was wildly popular is that it hit the right balance more perfectly than pretty much any WW book before it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 04-17-2017, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:26:55-07:00","id":1079802,"title":"","content":"I don't know how much the game will change now, but will it be compatible with the Dark Eras chapters that were already based on second edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:41:43-07:00","id":1079808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079802#post1079802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how much the game will change now, but will it be compatible with the Dark Eras chapters that were already based on second edition?</div> </div> </div> </div> The only one of those that we're compatible with David Hill's 2e changeling was London's, which is why I found Dark Eras disappointing, so much of the Changeling Mechanics just weren't compatible with Changeling 2e, now we don't know if any if it is compatible.<br /> <br /> Dark Eras should never have been released until all of the Settings had reached 2e, it was premature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T10:07:49-07:00","id":1079853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1060128-david-hill-has-left-opp-what-happens-to-changeling-now-changeling-is-still-happening?p=1079808#post1079808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Eras should never have been released until all of the Settings had reached 2e, it was premature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a chance. If anything, the Changeling eras shouldn't have been updated until Changeling 2e was actually out. Dark Eras was a huge win for OPP, it got people excited for the gamelines and it was one of their most successful kickstarters. If it weren't for Dark Eras, I probably wouldn't be playing CofD right now and would not care at all about Hunter or Mage. Given what a beauty of a game Mage 2e is, I'd say it came at exactly the right time.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT</b>: Also, the only era for Changeling era that wasn't 2e or partial 2e was Lily, Saber, Thorn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" t